==Enemy==
[[The Face]], but with legs. He has 1/2 the stats The Face has, but much more speed. Dashing Face is similar to [[Shy Boy]] due to his nature of attacking continuously and fast speed, but drops as much money as The Face upon death and has one more knockback than Shy Boy.

==Strategy==
The best way to defeat Dashing Face is to treat him as if it was a Shy Boy, but without any specific [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] weaknesses. Since he is [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]], Dashing Face has far fewer [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] and debuffs that can slow his progress. Instead, use plenty of meatshields with general attackers and if that isn't enough, [[Weaken|weaken]] him with [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Magica Cat]].

Attacker-wise, [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] along with their [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed]] [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|variants]] should work well. [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] are also effective against Dashing Face. [[:Category:Nuker-class Cats|Nukers]] will be worth your budget here since one-shotting or crippling him in 1 hit can give you more money than you spent on one unit.

When his running and chomping is put to an end, Dashing Face will drop as much cash as an ordinary Face does, so don't be afraid to use a lot of your budget to kill it. Although, this is not that possible in [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 18|Floor 18]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]], where you will probably be tight on cash until you kill the first or second Dashing Face.

